WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.650
All right, here's to a successful 
school festival concert.

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.650
<b>Anime Club</b>

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.520
Cheers!

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.530
Cheers!

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.530
Thank you for a successful school festival!
After-party

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.970
Great job, everyone!

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:12.510
Yeah, great job.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.030
Great job!

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.160
You hold after-parties when 
you finish an anime, too, huh?

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.150
They're held at rather lavish venues.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.290
Or so I've heard.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.800
It's like a festival at the 
end of the project, after all.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.910
I've heard they have bingo parties and stuff.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.050
They're supposed to be gorgeous.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:41.180
<b>Fight! 
Onotokisaka Academy 
Idol Club!</b>

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:41.180
<b>Good Work!</b>

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.400
I've seen them on social media,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.180
having cake with the 
characters printed on it.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.440
It's also a time for those 
who have few connections

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.060
with each other to come together.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.070
That sounds fun.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.070
I heard they have trouble 
deciding what to wear, though.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.760
And that arranging for the parties is hard.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.680
It's hard to work around the 
staff and cast's schedule.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.330
The popular ones must be really busy.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.210
I've heard that the writers 
feel completely out of place.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.710
Completely out of place?

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.340
A lot of time passes between when the 
script is written and the after-party.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.690
They're in a totally different 
mood from the rest of the staff

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.100
who'd just finished making the anime, huh?

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.220
No one needs the screenwriters.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.980
That's not true, I'm sure.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.390
The school president council 
hasn't said anything, huh?

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.100
I heard she got sick after 
the school festival.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.150
She hasn't come to school, either.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.240
Gaghflighehoyhoyfoobar.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.640
I guess I was hoping for too much,

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.000
thinking we could patch things up 
while emotions were running high.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:50.080
That anime short had me seriously pumped.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.880
I was hoping we could finish it to the end.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.750
The event was a blast.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.010
Let's just call it a win.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.760
It was worth the effort.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.740
Worth the effort, huh?

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:03.760
Yui-chan?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:08.160
I was just thinking, life doesn't 
really work out like in anime.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.020
Did something happen?

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:13.300
I can't jump the way I want to these days.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.900
Oh, your high jumps.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.330
I can't break my record.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.560
I'm doing the best I can, but...

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.790
Yeah?

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.910
At times like these, Musashisakai-senpai 
would be like, "Look at the saddle!"

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.590
That's an anime classic.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:30.540
Saddle?

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:35.000
It's from a club about a bike racing 
anime called <i>Nakimushi Saddle</i>.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:39.050
Watching them, your hands get 
all sweaty as you cheer them on.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:43.060
It's not about track club, but I 
think it could give you inspiration.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.140
I think I'll watch it.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.310
If you'd like...

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.950
I'll lend you my Blu-ray.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.000
Really?

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.190
Thanks.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.600
Yui-chan, you watch anime?

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.350
Yeah, I do, these days.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.150
I think you've influenced me.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.200
It's fun, once you start watching.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.320
Right?

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:11.320
Hina, Hina, Hina...

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.830
Yui-chan!

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.830
Hina! Hina!

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.830
Morning, Minoa.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.460
M-Morning.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.850
What was that song?

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:21.080
It's the Hina song from <i>Saddle</i>.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.170
The one Azemichi-kun sang.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.170
Hi!

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:28.540
Breathe to the rhythm of the shouts, and bam!

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.850
Thanks for the awesome song, Obata.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.580
This is thanks to the Anime Club, too.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.610
Hina! Hina! Hina!

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:37.860
Thanks.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.610
Y-You're welcome.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.010
Okay, see you in class.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.280
As long as it's being useful, I guess.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.160
<b>Anime Club</b>

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.160
A baseball anime?

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.190
We want advice...

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:55.670
...like you gave the track club.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.170
Please!

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:58.710
Um...

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.950
You've come to the right place.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:03.680
Passion!

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:04.680
Hard work!

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.080
Victory!

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.520
These are the things that sports 
anime are perfect for expressing.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:16.460
And thus sports themes are staple in anime.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:19.280
There are a ton of baseball classics,

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.690
including <i>Miracle Titans 
Mudou-kun</i> and <i>Ace of the Bench</i>.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:26.250
Being able to show off a lot of characters 
is one of the nice things about sports anime.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.080
You can have a perfect assortment 
of unique, attractive characters.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:32.200
It's nice that everyone's 
in matching uniforms, too.

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:33.790
There's a sense of camaraderie.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.080
Cosplaying them with your 
friends is great, too.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:41.570
Even the often-mocked, hyperbolic training 
scenes and impossible techniques

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:45.470
are perfectly fine handled in the style 
of a special ability battle anime.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:51.930
Take this!

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.960
Lightning mach ba—

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.890
Morning, Minoacchi.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:00.250
Um, Erika-senpai...

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.470
I'm not giving up!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.470
Huh...

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:05.040
It's Mudou-kun's Lighting Mach Ball.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:08.380
Shouldn't we stop him?

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:09.910
He's going to hurt himself.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.580
Morning!

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.410
I'm starting my trick throw training!

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.220
That's great.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.410
I'm glad we helped you out.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:26.350
Next club, please.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.680
Arisu-chan, what is this?

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.030
Isn't it amazing?

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.680
Everyone's asking for advice.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.100
A grudge practice match?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.480
You need to watch the <i>Fresh Prince 
of Tennis: Kanto Regionals</i>, then.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.190
Build your empire on a cool, collected mind.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.070
I get it.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.400
You can't win in the robot competition?

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.950
That's why you're a fool!

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.070
<i>Tengen Bakuha Guden Daran</i>!

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.300
Best everything with your drill!

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.330
Brother!

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.130
You don't have a single win yet?

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:01.930
Then <i>Slash Dunk</i> and <i>Tarako's 
Basketball</i> are for you.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:05.210
The game ends when you give up.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:09.720
I want to play basketball, Anime Club.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.520
Thank you!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.800
Giving advice...

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:12.850
Thank you!

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.970
When did you kids become so celebrated?

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.460
Neko-senpai...

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.520
Liquid Nitrogen

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.650
Behold... The Frozen World!

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:29.090
I'll destroy you, basket and all!

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.950
Hammer of Destruction!

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:36.780
If you want to be better at Mahjong, 
you need to watch <i>Shake</i>.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:38.750
Mahjong is fun.

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:40.990
You want to win the competition?

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:43.630
You need <i>Timbre! French Horn</i>.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:49.130
If you stand on a bridge and shout 
"I want to get better!" it'll be perfect.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.130
I hate it when it's noisy.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.390
Hey, it's a cat.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.400
Nyan-nyanko-sensei!

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.140
He looks just like Yabanyan.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.790
So cute!

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:56.790
Aww.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:58.110
Quit it.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.930
Bye-bye!

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.520
Bye-bye-nyan.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:06.400
Well, there's nothing wrong with 
helping people who need help.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.400
Right.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.980
I don't think there's anything wrong with it.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:12.910
It's helping people, and no one's getting hurt.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.450
True.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.410
I know, but...

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:21.140
Wait, you know what Neko-senpai 
is saying, Nakano-senpai?

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:21.790
Yeah.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:25.040
By the way, speaking of sports anime...

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.920
Repeating pans!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.300
Three times, at that.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.380
And sketch filters.

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:36.020
Don't forget the god rays, too.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:40.860
I have no idea what you 
two are talking about.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.550
Minoa!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:45.700
Yui-chan.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.640
I heard the Anime Club's huge right now.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:50.280
That's amazing.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.530
This?

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:56.900
The robotics club helped me out.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:00.360
It's amazing. It speeds up 
like crazy when you run.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.400
Apparently they took inspiration 
from anime for this, too.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.710
But isn't that cheating?

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.340
I think I can break my record now!

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.740
Okay, I'm getting back to practice.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.090
Dash mode.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.580
Vwoom!

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.930
Yui-chan!

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:25.140
Are you all right?

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:26.940
I'm fine.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.290
Ow...

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:31.800
Obata, that's enough!

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:35.950
<b>The Anime Club: Forever Snobs</b>

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:44.960
Vwoom!

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.410
Are you pumped for this 
week's <i>Show Up Rockin'</i>?

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:28.100
Sure.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:29.850
<i>Aww!</i>

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:33.220
You shouldn't neglect Dad.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.610
Hey, what kind of practice does your club do?

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:39.690
The lacrosse club?

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:41.310
Nothing special.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:45.120
We practice sprinting and 
swinging the stick and stuff.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:50.390
Would you ever, say, mod your stick 
so you could shoot really far?

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:53.250
No way, that would be cheating.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.880
That would be an anime, Minoa.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.070
I know, right?

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:09.830
The martial arts club's training grounds.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:12.420
It's coming along nicely.

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:15.150
The martial arts club's training grounds?

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:18.620
I heard they're going to duel 
at the top of that pyramid.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:21.200
Isn't that dangerous?

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.800
Look, Minoa, it's the Go Volleyball Club.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:27.120
Go Volleyball Club?!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.290
All right, begin!

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.710
The hand of God!

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:39.300
It looks like the Anime 
Club's advice is paying off.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.020
Yup.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:42.680
The whole school is brimming with life.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:45.530
There you all are.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:49.060
The robotics club is about do 
a test launch on its prototype.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.310
It's finally complete?!

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.090
Let's go watch it, Minoa.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:56.070
Wait, test launch?

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:01.380
All right.

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:06.060
King Sakaneko Legs-only Version, commence!

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:17.970
Sakaneko Academy's scientific 
prowess is unrivaled!

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:52.120
Isn't this bad?

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:10.760
Thank you.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:12.270
Something's wrong.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:17.520
Prototypes are supposed to be more 
capable than the mass-production units.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:20.250
It's a prototype. What can you do?

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.070
<b>Anime Club</b>

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.990
When do you think that robot 
will be finished, Minoa?

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:29.450
Huge news!

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:32.060
What is it, Sensei?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.420
We're getting a TV interview!

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:35.630
TV?

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:37.710
TV? You mean...

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:41.050
The thing that sends us anime?!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:45.090
Although it's just a local cable TV station.

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.490
They want to report on this unique school

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:51.270
that incorporates anime into its training.

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:55.350
That's splendid, Sensei.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.830
This is amazing, Minoa!

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.240
Y-Yeah.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:00.640
At last!

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:02.940
At last, our time has come!

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.610
We can finally win!

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.360
It's my TV debut.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:11.740
This beautiful, young light novel 
author might get a book deal.

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:14.040
How should I dress?

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.120
Should I cosplay?

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:16.800
Barbers!

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:18.250
I need to go to the barber shop.

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:24.210
But I shall have to conceal the power 
of my evil eye in front of the camera.

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:26.360
Autographs!

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.260
I need to think of an autograph!

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:35.270
<b>Anime Club</b>

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:35.270
I'll be heading home.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.400
Arisu-chan and the others seem really happy.

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:46.730
And the people in the other 
clubs are working hard.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.400
But...

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:54.410
Is it all so weird that you feel 
like you're the only sane one?

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:55.890
Yeah.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:59.420
But you aren't alone.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:03.260
You've always had someone by your side.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:06.760
Arisu-chan!

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.270
Arisu-chan!

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:10.820
Forget it!

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.030
Go have him cheer you up.

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:13.800
Him?

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:22.490
You left by yourself, so I got a bit worried.

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:30.220
Minoa-chan, there's something you 
gained in this club, isn't there?

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:34.850
Something I gained?

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.580
Arisu-chan, Miko-chan, the senpais...

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:43.340
Everyone loves anime, and I have 
friends that I can talk about it to.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.840
Lots of happy memories.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.130
That's right.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:52.590
Anime has the power to connect 
people and make them happy.

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:55.410
That's exactly what's happening now.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:16:00.640
Anime connected us to the people 
in the other clubs, too.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.480
And anime's making everyone happy.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.110
It's a happy ending.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:11.610
What you and the Anime Club 
did together wasn't a mistake.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:14.480
That's why we're getting an interview.

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:18.020
Yeah.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.170
Maybe you're right.

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:26.640
The Anime Club proposes incorporating

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:31.200
anime-style approaches 
to training in all clubs.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.010
It was my idea!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:39.010
Anime-inspired training 
appears absurd, at first,

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:42.890
but in order to break through your 
shell and exceed your limits,

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:46.780
you need a certain degree of daring.

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:49.780
That has always been my conviction.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:53.400
Free ideas, unrestrained by common sense.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:57.410
That's the greatest allure 
and strength of anime.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:00.410
Humanity knows no limits.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.290
The strength to believe we can go anywhere.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:06.880
That's the power of anime.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:10.330
That is what I have taught them every day.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.050
I did! It was all me!

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:33.000
Babababoom!

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:38.030
It's a new record.

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:40.800
Yay!

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.950
Congratulations, Yui-chan.

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:45.460
Thanks.

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:50.210
This is all thanks to the anime that 
you and your friends told me about.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:54.010
What you did wasn't a mistake.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:54.980
Wasn't a mistake...

00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:56.470
Wasn't a mistake...

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.430
Thank goodness for anime.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:03.600
This isn't much, but...

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.850
<b>Thank you</b>

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.850
Sakana Cable TV, Co.

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:06.850
No, I'd rather not.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.210
It's fine, Sensei.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.000
Let's just add it to our club funding.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:13.730
But...

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:18.680
We can buy another VHD deck.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:22.480
Why, thank you.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:29.500
All right.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.680
Let's call it a day.

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.130
Okay.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.240
What shall I watch when I get home?

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:37.510
I think I'll watch <i>Dirlish Bumper</i>.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:40.560
I like the protagonist's wacky personality.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.890
Her catch phrase...

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:44.430
We win.

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:45.890
It's from Tsubaki.

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:45.890
That's the one.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:52.690
Be careful

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.260
"Be careful"?

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:54.690
Of what?

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:59.700
I don't know what you're talking 
about, but hurry up and get better

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:06.820
The Anime Club is hereby...

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:08.710
...being shut down.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.280
Ignored?!

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.360
Sure.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:15.710
The club's about to get shut down.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.440
How many times has this happened now?

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:19.630
What is this, recycled content?

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:23.610
You won't be so indifferent for long!

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:24.760
Why, you ask?

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.730
Because it was this man...

00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:29.360
...who declared it!

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:33.480
Pri—

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.740
Principal!

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.650
Principal?

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:41.480
This man is?

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.980
This is my first time seeing him.

00:19:44.770 --> 00:19:46.340
What?!

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:49.750
You people have seen him at 
the school gate every day!

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.370
The school gate?

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.710
The artwork's starting to suck!

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:05.050
Guys...

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:12.060
To think I would step 
foot in here once again.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:16.360
Again?

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:19.780
It's an order from the principal this time.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:20.520
You don't get any notice.

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.560
You're out!

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:24.200
Th-This is tyranny!

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:26.830
You don't even have a reason to shut us down.

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:31.960
Sakaneko Academy Code Article 13 Section 2:

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:37.840
"A club shall not receive money for its 
activities outside of the academy's allocations."

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:40.000
Receiving money?!

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:43.040
Wh-When did you guys do that?!

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.430
We didn't!

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:45.890
Come on.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:50.470
Sensei, you totally took money.

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:55.600
President, they did indeed take

00:20:56.210 --> 00:21:00.730
gratuities from the TV crew.

00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:03.050
N-Nakano...

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:07.550
Oh, you already bought the deck.

00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:09.870
Sensei!

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.840
Please don't use club funds 
without saying anything!

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:14.370
Look who's talking.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.940
The Anime Club is to be shut down.

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:22.630
Gomon-sensei is suspended from duty.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.360
No!

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:31.020
Good work, Nakano-kun.

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:33.040
Nakano-senpai!

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.020
Why?

00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:41.900
Aurora!

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.410
You screwed us over, Aurora!

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:51.910
Please don't call me that.

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.560
Never forgive a traitor.

00:23:30.560 --> 00:23:33.330
That is the code of the Cat Knighthood.

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:35.770
Next episode, someone changes their ways?

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:39.320
Whose name does the traitor know?

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:43.680
Watch Again
Gataris
